{"slug":"valid-palindrome","title":"Valid Palindrome","level":"Easy","summary":"After lower-casing letters and dropping every character that is not a letter or digit, does the string read the same both ways?","method":"isPalindrome","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["\"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"race a car\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\" \""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"0P\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"ab_a\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\".,\""],"out":"true"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#5:b5fae2c14238b978\"","perf":{"label":"a 200,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(200000, \"ab ,.AB09\");"},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"valid-palindrome-ignoring-non-alphanumerics-and-case"},
{"slug":"remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array","title":"Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array","level":"Easy","summary":"Given a sorted array, keep one copy of each value at the front, in order, in place, and return how many unique values there are. The judge prints k and the first k elements.","method":"removeDuplicates","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"int","call":"int[] a = BCB.IA($0); int k = s.removeDuplicates(a); Object r = new Object[] { k, Arrays.copyOf(a, Math.max(0, Math.min(k, a.length))) };","tests":[{"in":["[1,1,2]"],"out":"[2,[1,2]]"},{"in":["[0,0,1,1,1,2,2,3,3,4]"],"out":"[5,[0,1,2,3,4]]"},{"in":["[7]"],"out":"[1,[7]]"},{"in":["[-3,-3,-3]"],"out":"[1,[-3]]"},{"in":["[1,2,3,4]"],"out":"[4,[1,2,3,4]]"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#693:867ab729ef99700\"","perf":{"label":"n = 30,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.sorted(30000, -100, 100);","call":"int k = s.removeDuplicates(a0); Object r = new Object[] { k, Arrays.copyOf(a0, Math.max(0, Math.min(k, a0.length))) };"},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"two-pointers"},
{"slug":"move-zeroes","title":"Move Zeroes","level":"Easy","summary":"Move every 0 to the end of the array in place, keeping the other values in their original order. The judge prints the array after your call.","method":"moveZeroes","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"void","output":0,"tests":[{"in":["[0,1,0,3,12]"],"out":"[1,3,12,0,0]"},{"in":["[0]"],"out":"[0]"},{"in":["[1,2,3]"],"out":"[1,2,3]"},{"in":["[0,0,1]"],"out":"[1,0,0]"},{"in":["[4,0,-2,0,0,7]"],"out":"[4,-2,7,0,0,0]"}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"move-zeroes-keep-the-order-of-non-zeros"},
{"slug":"squares-of-a-sorted-array","title":"Squares of a Sorted Array","level":"Easy","summary":"Given a sorted array that may contain negatives, return the squares of its values in sorted order — ideally in O(n).","method":"sortedSquares","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"int[]","tests":[{"in":["[-4,-1,0,3,10]"],"out":"[0,1,9,16,100]"},{"in":["[-7,-3,2,3,11]"],"out":"[4,9,9,49,121]"},{"in":["[-5]"],"out":"[25]"},{"in":["[-3,-2,-1]"],"out":"[1,4,9]"},{"in":["[0,0,1]"],"out":"[0,0,1]"}],"lesson":"two-pointers"},
{"slug":"two-sum-ii-input-array-is-sorted","title":"Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted","level":"Medium","summary":"In a 1-indexed sorted array, find the two positions whose values add up to target (exactly one answer exists) using O(1) extra space. Return them as [index1, index2].","method":"twoSum","params":[["int[]","numbers"],["int","target"]],"returns":"int[]","tests":[{"in":["[2,7,11,15]","9"],"out":"[1,2]"},{"in":["[2,3,4]","6"],"out":"[1,3]"},{"in":["[-1,0]","-1"],"out":"[1,2]"},{"in":["[1,2,3,4,4,9,56,90]","8"],"out":"[4,5]"},{"in":["[-10,-3,0,5,9]","6"],"out":"[2,5]"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#12:7b6d83835f4a0be7\"","perf":{"label":"n = 30,000","gen":"int[] a0 = new int[30000]; for (int i = 0; i < a0.length; i++) a0[i] = 4 * i - 60000; a0[5000] += 1; a0[25000] += 1; int a1 = a0[5000] + a0[25000];"},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"two-pointers"},
{"slug":"container-with-most-water","title":"Container With Most Water","level":"Medium","summary":"height[i] is a vertical line at x = i. Pick two lines that, with the x-axis, hold the most water, and return that area.","method":"maxArea","params":[["int[]","height"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]"],"out":"49"},{"in":["[1,1]"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[4,3,2,1,4]"],"out":"16"},{"in":["[1,2,1]"],"out":"2"},{"in":["[0,0,0,5]"],"out":"0"},{"in":["[2,3,10,5,7,8,9]"],"out":"36"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#9:b136e4307d1c97f7\"","perf":{"label":"n = 100,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(100000, 0, 10000);"},"refMs":3}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"container-with-most-water"},
{"slug":"3sum","title":"3Sum","level":"Medium","summary":"Return every unique triplet of values (from different positions) that sums to zero. Triplets may be in any order.","method":"threeSum","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"List<List<Integer>>","check":"any-order-deep","tests":[{"in":["[-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]"],"out":"[[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]"},{"in":["[0,1,1]"],"out":"[]"},{"in":["[0,0,0]"],"out":"[[0,0,0]]"},{"in":["[0,0,0,0]"],"out":"[[0,0,0]]"},{"in":["[-2,0,1,1,2]"],"out":"[[-2,0,2],[-2,1,1]]"},{"in":["[3,-2,1,0,-1,2,-3]"],"out":"[[-3,0,3],[-3,1,2],[-2,-1,3],[-2,0,2],[-1,0,1]]"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#348526:502d21137a04fca9\"","perf":{"label":"n = 3,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(3000, -100000, 100000);"},"refMs":24}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"3sum--fix-one-two-pointer-the-rest"},
{"slug":"sort-colors","title":"Sort Colors","level":"Medium","summary":"The array holds only 0, 1 and 2. Sort it in place in one pass without a library sort. The judge prints the array after your call.","method":"sortColors","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"void","output":0,"tests":[{"in":["[2,0,2,1,1,0]"],"out":"[0,0,1,1,2,2]"},{"in":["[2,0,1]"],"out":"[0,1,2]"},{"in":["[1]"],"out":"[1]"},{"in":["[2,2,0,0]"],"out":"[0,0,2,2]"},{"in":["[1,0,2,1,0,2,1]"],"out":"[0,0,1,1,1,2,2]"}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"sort-colors--three-pointers-dutch-national-flag"},
{"slug":"trapping-rain-water","title":"Trapping Rain Water","level":"Hard","summary":"height[i] is the height of a bar of width 1. After rain, how much water is trapped between the bars?","method":"trap","params":[["int[]","height"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]"],"out":"6"},{"in":["[4,2,0,3,2,5]"],"out":"9"},{"in":["[1]"],"out":"0"},{"in":["[3,2,1]"],"out":"0"},{"in":["[5,0,5]"],"out":"5"},{"in":["[2,0,2,0,3,1,4]"],"out":"6"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#10:1c9fbdb6a6c29d4a\"","perf":{"label":"n = 20,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(20000, 0, 100000);"},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"two-pointers","anchor":"trapping-rain-water-hard"}
]
